    "mcpTools": [
      {
        "name": "ha_history_get_current_time",
        "description": "Returns the current date and time from the Home Assistant server (Oslo).\nCall this before making any time-based query when the user uses a relative or named time\nexpression: \"last month\", \"this winter\", \"yesterday\", \"last year\", \"in april\", \"recently\".\nDo not rely on your training data to infer the current date — it will often be wrong.\nSkip only if an absolute ISO date range has already been stated in this conversation."
      },
      {
        "name": "ha_history_list_entities",
        "description": "Lists Oslo sensors that have historical data available.\nEach result includes the entity_id, friendly name, room/area, unit, and sensor type.\nCall this to find the correct entity_id before querying any sensor you don't already know.\nSkip only if the entity_id was already resolved earlier in this conversation.\nAlso use for explicit sensor discovery or when a previous call returned an ambiguous match.\nBinary sensors (motion, doors, presence) require domain=\"binary_sensor\" — they have no\nstatistics so they won't appear in a plain search without specifying that domain."
      },
      {
        "name": "ha_history_get_sensor_stats",
        "description": "Computes statistics for a Oslo sensor measuring instantaneous values:\ntemperature, humidity, CO₂, pressure, illuminance, or power draw in Watts.\nUse for: \"What was the lowest temperature last night?\", \"Average humidity in April?\",\n\"Warmest day last summer?\", \"How many days above 25°C?\", \"Which days had frost?\",\n\"At what time of day is it usually hottest?\", \"Which day of the week is most humid?\"\nDo NOT use for energy consumption (kWh) → use ha_history_get_consumption.\nDo NOT use for event counting → use ha_history_detect_sessions."
      },
      {
        "name": "ha_history_get_consumption",
        "description": "Calculates how much energy, water, gas, or other resource was consumed or produced\nin Oslo over a time period.\nUse for: \"How much electricity did the car charger use in February?\",\n\"Total electricity last month?\", \"Solar production last week?\",\n\"Daily energy usage last week\", \"Compare grid import this April vs last April\",\n\"Which days used more than 10 kWh?\"\nAlways returns consumption (the change over the period), never raw meter readings.\nDo NOT use for instantaneous sensors (temperature, power in Watts) → use ha_history_get_sensor_stats."
      },
      {
        "name": "ha_history_detect_sessions",
        "description": "Detects and counts discrete events or activity sessions from Oslo sensor history.\nUse for: \"How many times was the car charged in February?\",\n\"How many times did the washing machine run last week?\",\n\"How many times was the front door opened?\",\n\"Was there any motion in the garage overnight?\",\n\"What was the longest charging session last month?\",\n\"What time did the last person go to bed each night this week?\" (use group_by=\"day\")\nFor numeric sensors (power in W): uses long-term hourly statistics — full date range.\nFor binary sensors (motion, door): uses state history — limited to ~10 days.\nReturns: event count, total duration, compact session list, or daily summary (with group_by=\"day\")."
      }
    ]
  },
